   "date": "2014-06-11T17:11:38Z",
   "subject": "Rstan running so slow for a GEV model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">   My model compiles good and can run. But it is very slow and it always get like this &quot;Iteration: 1/10000 [ 0%] (warmup)&quot;. <div>I get the initial values from in2extRemes package which are reasonable. I stop the running and check the results which reveals that the first several iterations are near to initial values and then change so much. Here is my simple model. Can someone help with that? Thank you!<div><br></div><div><div>data {</div><div>    int&lt;lower=0&gt; n;</div><div>    vector[n] t;</div><div>    real y[n];</div><div>}</div><div><br></div><div>parameters {</div><div>  real mu;</div><div><br></div><div>  real&lt;lower=0&gt; sigma;</div><div><br></div><div>  real xi;</div><div>}</div><div><br></div><div>model {</div><div>  real z[n];</div><div>  for (i in 1:n){</div><div>      z[i] &lt;- 1 + (y[i] - mu) * xi / sigma;</div><div>  }</div><div><br></div><div>  if (xi==0){</div><div>  y ~ gumbel(mu,sigma);</div><div>   }else{</div><div>  increment_log_prob(log(1 / sigma) - (1 + 1/xi)*log(z[n]) - pow(z[n],-1/xi));</div><div>  }</div><div><br></div><div>}</div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "l6fhZXUvTd8J",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2014-06-11T19:45:16Z",
   "subject": "Re: Rstan running so slow for a GEV model",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Wednesday, June 11, 2014 1:11:38 PM UTC-4, Hang Zeng wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">   My model compiles good and can run. But it is very slow and it always get like this &quot;Iteration: 1/10000 [ 0%] (warmup)&quot;. <div>I get the initial values from in2extRemes package which are reasonable. I stop the running and check the results which reveals that the first several iterations are near to initial values and then change so much. Here is my simple model. Can someone help with that? Thank you!</div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>For distributions like the GEV where the support depends on the parameter values, you have to be clever with the declarations in the parameters section. Otherwise, you get into a situation where what Stan thinks are valid parameter values have zero or undefined density values. In your case, it would be something like<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><div><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span></div><div><span style=\"color:#000\">   vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span></div><div><span style=\"color:#000\">   real y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span></div><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>transformed data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real min_y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real max_y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  min_y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> min</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  max_y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> max</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real xi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">if_else</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xi </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> min_y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> negative_infinity</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>       upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">if_else</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xi </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> infinity</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> max_y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xi </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    z </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xi </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    increment_log_prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sigma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> pow</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">));</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  <br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// priors on xi, sigma, and mu</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Ben<br><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
